# RelayKit

RelayKit is a local OpenAI-compatible gateway that routes requests to OAuth-authenticated CLI providers (OpenCode, Claude, Gemini, Codex, Ollama, and more) and exposes a single base URL for any app that supports OpenAI-compatible endpoints.

## Quick start (macOS/Linux)

```bash
cd /path/to/RelayKit
./scripts/install.sh
./scripts/run.sh
```

Open the local UI at:
- http://127.0.0.1:11435/ui

OpenAI-compatible base URL:
- http://127.0.0.1:11435/v1

If your app runs inside Docker, use:
- http://host.docker.internal:11435/v1

## What works today

- OpenAI-compatible `/v1/models`
- OpenAI-compatible `/v1/chat/completions`
- Streaming responses
- Auto-detect OpenCode CLI and list models
- Route by model prefix:
  - `claude:...` -> Anthropic via OpenCode
  - `gemini:...` -> Google via OpenCode
  - `codex:...` or `openai:...` -> OpenAI via OpenCode
  - `ollama:...` -> Ollama via OpenCode (if configured)

## Provider detection

RelayKit detects installed CLIs and lists them in the UI. Today, OpenCode is used as the primary backend because it already supports OAuth across multiple providers.

If you want to force a specific backend later, set:

```bash
export CLIBRIDGE_BACKEND=opencode
```

## Desktop UI (Tauri)

A minimal desktop UI is included in `apps/desktop`.

```bash
cd apps/desktop
npm install
npm run tauri dev
```

